<header><p class="st-kicker">sultanate · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Sultanate of Singora</h1><p class="st-meta">1605 CE – 1680 CE (approx.) · capital Songkhla</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Muslim port sultanate at Songkhla on the Thai peninsula that defied Ayutthaya in the 17th century before being destroyed in 1680.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Around 1605 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dato-mogol">Dato Mogol</a>, a Muslim leader said to be of Persian or Malay origin, established a fortified port at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songkhla">Singora</a>, present-day Songkhla, on the east coast of the peninsula. It grew under his son Sulaiman, who declared independence from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> around 1642.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songkhla">Singora</a> prospered from trade in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepper">pepper</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tin">tin</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a>, attracting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> and English merchants. Its rulers built strong fortifications on the hills above the town and repelled several Siamese expeditions in the mid 17th century. The population included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malays">Malays</a>, Thais and Chinese, and the sultans were Muslims.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Mustafa, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narai">King Narai</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya Kingdom</a> sent a large force that destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songkhla">Singora</a> in 1680. The ruling family was spared and resettled; Sulaiman's descendants served Siam as officials, and the town was later refounded across the lagoon. The sultan's tomb survives at Hua Khao Daeng.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sultanate-of-singora.jpg" alt="Sultanate of Singora" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Chainwit.Derived from a work by user:Hdamm · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sultanate_of_Singora_maps_EN.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1605 CE – 1680 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>sultanate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Songkhla</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Dato Mogol, Sulaiman, Mustafa</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malay</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Thailand</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Songkhla Sultanate, Singgora</dd></dl></aside></div>

